limitations_reported:
- "the interest of individuals was not assessed directly, no conclusion cannot be drawn at this time"; future studies combining neuroimaging and assessment of interests needed;
- Effect of OT not assessed under other social contexts — future studies with different contexts needed to confirm context-independent effect;
- "other" partner was unfamiliar (stranger) — effect of OT on prosocial behavior toward strangers is mixed; future studies could include familiarity factor;
- Working memory not directly measured — cannot examine whether working memory interacts with conditions;
- Proportions of individualists and prosocial individuals in PL and OT groups were unbalanced and limited;
- More trials might be needed to better capture the learning process in Study 2's more demanding task

